Chapter: SmpCores

 The multi-core boot, checked from inside the guest.

 Cell 4088 holds the core count, written by the virtual machine before
 boot. Cell 4080 is the ready counter: the boot processor clears it,
 sends INIT and two start-up interrupts, and each application processor
 that comes up adds one to the counter with a locked add before it
 halts. So the counter is written only by application processors, and
 only by ones that got far enough to execute guest instructions.

 That is the whole point of this test. A core the hypervisor has
 created, configured and reported as started has still not necessarily
 run a single instruction of ours -- for a long time none of them had,
 and the host was quietly incrementing this counter on their behalf,
 which made a dead core look like a live one. The counter is honest
 evidence now, and reading back one less than the core count means every
 application processor is genuinely executing guest code.

Section: Probe

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("cores: " & show (atomic-load 4088))
    print-line-uni ("aps checked in: " & show (atomic-load 4080))
    print-line-uni (if atomic-load 4080 == atomic-load 4088 - 1
                    then "every ap executed guest code"
                    else "AP DID NOT RUN")
  end
